# Successive release bumps change current examples, never historical version boundaries.
exec git init -q -b main
exec git add assets README.md site docs
exec perl $ASSETS/../scripts/set-version.pl 0.1.7
exec perl $ASSETS/../scripts/set-version.pl 0.1.8
cmp assets/framework/rules.md rules.want
cmp README.md readme.want
cmp site/src/docs/cli/version.md version.want
cmp docs/cli/interface.md interface.want
cmp docs/cli/git-checkpoint-implementation-plan.md history.want

# Invalid input fails before writing files.
! exec perl $ASSETS/../scripts/set-version.pl 0.1
stderr 'usage:'
cmp assets/framework/rules.md rules.want

-- assets/framework/rules.md --
# Framework rules
Framework version: 0.1.6
-- README.md --
git commit -m "chore: initialize solomonar 0.1.6"
Delivered in v0.1.6; CLI 0.1.6 and earlier used an older schema.
-- site/src/docs/cli/version.md --
solomonar 0.1.6
project   framework 0.1.6 · registry schema 2
In v0.1.6, extensions are chosen at init.
The v0.1.6 catalog holds go.
CLI 0.1.6 rejects a newer schema; Copilot 0.1.6 was tested.
-- docs/cli/interface.md --
{"cli": "0.1.6", "framework": "0.1.6", "project_framework": "0.1.6", "framework_version": "0.1.6"}
CLI 0.1.5 and earlier read schema 1; schema 2 shipped in v0.1.6.
-- docs/cli/git-checkpoint-implementation-plan.md --
Status: delivered in v0.1.6.
Framework 0.1.6 and earlier used a different contract.
-- rules.want --
# Framework rules
Framework version: 0.1.8
-- readme.want --
git commit -m "chore: initialize solomonar 0.1.8"
Delivered in v0.1.6; CLI 0.1.6 and earlier used an older schema.
-- version.want --
solomonar 0.1.8
project   framework 0.1.8 · registry schema 2
In v0.1.8, extensions are chosen at init.
The v0.1.8 catalog holds go.
CLI 0.1.6 rejects a newer schema; Copilot 0.1.6 was tested.
-- interface.want --
{"cli": "0.1.8", "framework": "0.1.8", "project_framework": "0.1.8", "framework_version": "0.1.8"}
CLI 0.1.5 and earlier read schema 1; schema 2 shipped in v0.1.6.
-- history.want --
Status: delivered in v0.1.6.
Framework 0.1.6 and earlier used a different contract.
